#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:2
msgid "Skip or cancel builds based on conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:4
msgid ""
"Read the Docs provides two mechanisms to avoid running unnecessary "
"documentation builds, saving build time and resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:7
msgid "Skip a build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:8
msgid ""
"The build is **never triggered**. Use :doc:`automation rules </automation-"
"rules>` with webhook filters to decide, before anything runs, whether a push "
"or pull request should build at all. This is the recommended approach "
"whenever it's available for your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:13
msgid "Cancel a build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:14
msgid ""
"The build is **triggered as usual**, and one of your commands exits with the "
"special exit code ``183`` to cancel it. Use this when your Git provider "
"doesn't support webhook filters, or when your condition requires shell logic "
"at build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:22
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:25
msgid "When to avoid building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:27
msgid ""
"There are several scenarios where you might want to avoid documentation "
"builds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:29
msgid "**Save resources on irrelevant changes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:30
msgid ""
"Avoid builds when changes don't affect documentation, such as changes only "
"to source code, tests, or CI configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:33
msgid "**Avoid redundant builds**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:34
msgid ""
"Avoid builds for draft pull requests, work-in-progress branches, or commits "
"with specific markers like ``[skip ci]`` in the commit message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:37
msgid "**Conditional documentation updates**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:38
msgid ""
"Only build documentation when specific files or directories are modified, "
"such as the ``docs/`` folder or configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:41
msgid "**Branch-specific logic**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:42
msgid ""
"Avoid builds on certain branches that don't require documentation updates, "
"such as experimental or development branches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:46
msgid "Skip builds with automation rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:48
msgid ""
"Automation rules with a ``Trigger build for version`` action let you filter "
"which webhook events trigger a build. You can match on the changed files, "
"the commit message, or the pull request labels. When no build rule matches, "
"the build is skipped: it doesn't appear in your build history and doesn't "
"consume any build time."
msgstr ""

