#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:80
msgid "Cancel builds with exit code 183"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:83
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:85
msgid ""
"When any command in your build process exits with the special exit code "
"``183``, Read the Docs will immediately cancel the build. The build will be "
"marked as *cancelled* and will not consume build time or resources beyond "
"that point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:89
msgid "Why exit code 183?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:91
msgid ""
"The exit code 183 was chosen because it represents the word \"skip\" encoded "
"in ASCII."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:93
msgid ""
">>> sum(list(\"skip\".encode(\"ascii\")))\n"
"439\n"
">>> 439 % 256  # Unix exit codes are limited to 0-255\n"
"183"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:100
msgid ""
"The 256 modulo operation is necessary because `Unix exit codes are limited "
"to 0-255 <https://tldp.org/LDP/abs/html/exitcodes.html>`_, and any value "
"larger than 255 is automatically reduced by taking the modulo 256."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:104
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:106
msgid ""
"The following examples demonstrate common use cases for cancelling builds. "
"All examples use the :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs` configuration key in "
"your ``.readthedocs.yaml`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:111
msgid "Cancel builds when documentation files haven't changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:115
msgid ""
"If your project is connected through the GitHub App, :ref:`skipping the "
"build with an automation rule <guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds:Skip "
"builds with automation rules>` is the recommended approach. Automation rules "
"avoid triggering the build at all, whereas the approach below cancels a "
"build that is already running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:120
msgid ""
"This example cancels pull request builds when there are no changes to "
"documentation-related files compared to the ``main`` branch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:123
#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:153
#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:176
#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:198
msgid ".readthedocs.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:123
msgid ""
"version: 2\n"
"build:\n"
"  os: \"ubuntu-22.04\"\n"
"  tools:\n"
"    python: \"3.12\"\n"
"  jobs:\n"
"    post_checkout:\n"
"      # Cancel building pull requests when there aren't changes in the docs "
"directory or YAML file.\n"
"      # If there are no changes (git diff exits with 0) we force the command "
"to return with 183.\n"
"      # This is a special exit code on Read the Docs that will cancel the "
"build immediately.\n"
"      - |\n"
"        if [ \"$READTHEDOCS_VERSION_TYPE\" = \"external\" ] && git diff --"
"quiet origin/main -- docs/ .readthedocs.yaml;\n"
"        then\n"
"          exit 183;\n"
"        fi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:142
msgid "You can customize this example by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:144
msgid ""
"Adding more paths to check: ``docs/ .readthedocs.yaml requirements/docs.txt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:145
msgid ""
"Checking against a different branch: ``origin/develop`` instead of ``origin/"
"main``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:146
msgid ""
"Using different comparison operators to check for specific file patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:149
msgid "Cancel builds based on commit message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:151
msgid ""
"This example cancels builds when the commit message contains ``[skip ci]`` "
"or ``[ci skip]``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:153
msgid ""
"version: 2\n"
"build:\n"
"  os: \"ubuntu-22.04\"\n"
"  tools:\n"
"    python: \"3.12\"\n"
"  jobs:\n"
"    post_checkout:\n"
"      # Use `git log` to check if the latest commit contains \"skip ci\",\n"
"      # in that case exit the command with 183 to cancel the build\n"
"      - (git --no-pager log --pretty=\"tformat:%s -- %b\" -1 | paste -s -d "
"\" \" | grep -viq \"skip ci\") || exit 183"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:167
msgid ""
"This pattern is commonly used in CI/CD systems to skip builds for "
"administrative commits, such as version bumps or documentation typos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:171
msgid "Cancel builds for specific branch patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:173
msgid ""
"This example cancels builds for branches that match certain patterns, such "
"as personal development branches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:176
msgid ""
"version: 2\n"
"build:\n"
"  os: \"ubuntu-22.04\"\n"
"  tools:\n"
"    python: \"3.12\"\n"
"  jobs:\n"
"    post_checkout:\n"
"      # Cancel builds for branches starting with \"dev/\" or \"experiment/"
"\"\n"
"      - |\n"
"        if echo \"$READTHEDOCS_GIT_IDENTIFIER\" | grep -qE \"^(dev|"
"experiment)/\"; then\n"
"          exit 183;\n"
"        fi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:193
msgid "Cancel builds based on file types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:195
msgid ""
"This example cancels builds when all changes are to non-documentation files, "
"such as only images or data files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:198
msgid ""
"version: 2\n"
"build:\n"
"  os: \"ubuntu-22.04\"\n"
"  tools:\n"
"    python: \"3.12\"\n"
"  jobs:\n"
"    post_checkout:\n"
"      # Cancel if only non-documentation files changed (e.g., only images or "
"data files)\n"
"      - |\n"
"        if [ \"$READTHEDOCS_VERSION_TYPE\" = \"external\" ]; then\n"
"          # Get list of changed files\n"
"          CHANGED_FILES=$(git diff --name-only origin/main)\n"
"          # Check if any changed files are documentation-related.\n"
"          # If ALL files are non-documentation (grep finds no documentation "
"files),\n"
"          # then we cancel the build by exiting with 183.\n"
"          if ! echo \"$CHANGED_FILES\" | grep -qE \"\\.(rst|md|py|yaml|yml|"
"txt|toml)$\"; then\n"
"            exit 183;\n"
"          fi\n"
"        fi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:222
msgid "Best practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:224
msgid ""
"When implementing build cancellation logic, consider these best practices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:226
msgid "**Test your conditions locally**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:227
msgid ""
"Before deploying cancellation logic, test your bash conditions locally to "
"ensure they work as expected. Remember that the condition failing will "
"cancel your build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:230
msgid "**Be specific with your conditions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:231
msgid ""
"Write clear and specific conditions to avoid accidentally cancelling builds "
"that should run. Overly broad conditions might prevent important "
"documentation updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:234
msgid "**Document your cancellation logic**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:235
msgid ""
"Add comments in your ``.readthedocs.yaml`` file explaining why builds are "
"cancelled and under what conditions. This helps future maintainers "
"understand the configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:238
msgid "**Consider the impact on pull requests**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:239
msgid ""
"If you cancel builds on pull requests, reviewers won't have preview "
"documentation. Make sure this aligns with your team's review process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:242
msgid "**Use environment variables**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:243
msgid ""
"Leverage :doc:`Read the Docs environment variables </reference/environment-"
"variables>` like ``READTHEDOCS_VERSION_TYPE`` to make your conditions more "
"precise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:247
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:249
msgid ""
"Be aware of these limitations when cancelling builds with exit code ``183``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:251
msgid "**No partial cancellation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:252
msgid ""
"Once a build is cancelled with exit code 183, the entire build stops "
"immediately. You cannot selectively skip only certain parts of the build "
"process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:255
msgid "**Not available in configuration file**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:256
msgid ""
"You cannot cancel builds using conditions in the ``.readthedocs.yaml`` "
"configuration syntax itself. All logic must be implemented in bash commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:259
msgid "**Build is counted as cancelled**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:260
msgid ""
"Cancelled builds appear in your build history as *cancelled*, not as "
"successful. This is different from builds skipped by automation rules, which "
"never appear in the build history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:263
msgid "**No failure notifications are sent**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:264
msgid ""
"When a build is cancelled via exit code ``183``, Read the Docs does not send "
"``build:failed`` webhook notifications or failure emails for it. The build "
"is treated as intentionally cancelled rather than failed. Note that a "
"``build:triggered`` webhook may still have been delivered earlier, before "
"the build command had a chance to exit with ``183``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:270
msgid "**Pull request status is reported as successful**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds.rst:271
msgid ""
"When a commit status is sent to your Git provider (for pull request builds), "
"it is reported as successful so that the pull request is not blocked from "
"merging."
msgstr ""

